                <pb facs="0527" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v19/pg501"/>

                <head>255. Letter From Prime Minister Nehru to President Kennedy<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d255-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>New Delhi</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-02-16">February 16,
                        1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d255-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d255-f1-content">
                <p>[Source: Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Countries Series, India, Nehru
                    Correspondence, 2/11/63-3/31/63. No classification marking. According to a
                    February 27 memorandum from William Brubeck to McGeorge Bundy, the letter was
                    delivered to the White House on February 18 by Ambassador B.K. Nehru. (Ibid.)
                    This letter has not been declassified by the Indian Government. In his biography
                    of Prime Minister Nehru, Gopal states regarding this letter: “It was now Nehru’s
                    turn to complain that Pakistan was not wholly serious and not anxious to come to
                    an agreement.” (Gopal, Jawarharlal Nehru, Vol. 3, p. 258)]</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
